---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";

const updaterConfig = `{
  "plugins": {
    "updater": {
      "pubkey": "",
      "endpoints": []
    }
  }
}`;
---

<DocLayout lang="en" page="docs/release" eyebrow="Build and updates" title="Build, release, and updater status" intro="Opaline is in public alpha. Release builds are intended for testing and early feedback." next={[{ href: "/download", label: "Download alpha" }, { href: "/docs/roadmap", label: "Roadmap" }]}>
  <section>
    <h2>Current release</h2>
    <p>The current release is <a href="https://github.com/miqiv99/opaline/releases/tag/v0.1.2" rel="noreferrer">v0.1.2 on GitHub</a>. Do not guess asset names on the website; use the Release page as the source of truth.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Windows and macOS Apple Silicon assets are available for v0.1.2.</li>
      <li>Windows remains the primary active development target; macOS packages are built and tested on macOS.</li>
      <li>Linux support is future-facing until explicitly tested and documented.</li>
      <li>Unsigned or unnotarized packages may trigger platform warnings.</li>
      <li>Back up your workspace before testing with important notes.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>v0.1.2 editor updates</h2>
    <p>v0.1.2 improves editor infrastructure for later AI note generation and richer editing workflows.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A unified editor command registry is shared by toolbar actions, context menus, slash commands, the command palette, and future AI flows.</li>
      <li>Slash commands and the command palette cover common formatting, block, and insert operations.</li>
      <li>The AI editing protocol now includes command descriptors, JSON schema validation, permissions, preview metadata, confirmation gates, risk metadata, history-snapshot hooks, and rollback hooks.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Local build commands</h2>
    <pre><code>npm install
npm run tauri:dev
npm run tauri:build</code></pre>
    <p>Tauri bundle outputs are written under the target-specific release bundle directory, such as <code>src-tauri/target/release/bundle/</code> or <code>src-tauri/target/aarch64-apple-darwin/release/bundle/</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Manual updater status</h2>
    <p>Settings includes a manual "check for updates" flow. Opaline checks only when the user clicks the update button, and installing an available update requires a second explicit confirmation.</p>
    <p>The active updater configuration points at GitHub Releases. Current signed update metadata for v0.1.2 is tracked in the repository under <code>release-assets/v0.1.2/latest.json</code>.</p>
    <p>Keep <code>plugins.updater</code> as an object. Do not set it to <code>null</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>{updaterConfig}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Before enabling public updates</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Generate and protect the private Tauri updater signing key outside the repository.</li>
      <li>Upload the installer or app archive, matching <code>.sig</code>, and a real <code>latest.json</code> that points at existing assets.</li>
      <li>Test update installation with a non-essential workspace before announcing an update.</li>
      <li>Do not enable automatic background installation during public alpha.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
